{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lg0yuk7k","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 1 Offline","year":2007,"examDate":2007,"subject":"physics","chapter":"laws-of-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"friction-force","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"ptwo-particles-of-mass-m-each-are-tied-at-the-ends-of-a-li-jee-advanced-physics-motion-otgeix4wf1rlycli","content":"<p>Two particles of mass m each are tied at the ends of a light string of length 2a. The whole system is kept on a frictionless horizontal surface with the string held tight so that each mass is at a distance 'a' form the centre P (as shown in the figure). Now, the mid-point of the string is pulled vertically upwards with a small but constant force F. As a result, the particles move towards each other on the surface. The magnitude of acceleration, with the separation between them becomes 2x, is</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mggcb828/b81c65c2-b6b5-4f11-b91d-b4b6df612cee/8dbac900-a35d-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcb829.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1mggcb828/b81c65c2-b6b5-4f11-b91d-b4b6df612cee/8dbac900-a35d-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcb829.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Laws of Motion Question 9 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1mggcb828/b81c65c2-b6b5-4f11-b91d-b4b6df612cee/8dbac900-a35d-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcb829.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1mggcb828/b81c65c2-b6b5-4f11-b91d-b4b6df612cee/8dbac900-a35d-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcb829.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mggcb828/b81c65c2-b6b5-4f11-b91d-b4b6df612cee/8dbac900-a35d-11f0-b814-0f72f73fa4cf/file-jaoe38c1mggcb829.